    {
      "id": "r20261029-a02",
      "title": "The Return of the Train",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "For many years, trains were considered old-fashioned. Planes were faster and cars were more convenient. But today, trains are making a comeback in many parts of the world.",
        "One reason is the environment. A train journey produces far less pollution per passenger than a flight. Another reason is comfort. On a train, you can walk around, work at a table, and arrive in the city center instead of an airport far outside town. High-speed trains can now travel between many cities faster than the total time of a flight, once you count airport check-in and travel to the airport.",
        "Governments are listening. Countries in Europe and Asia are building new high-speed lines and reopening night trains with beds. For travelers who want a relaxed and greener way to move, the train is back on the menu."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "considered": "dianggap",
        "convenient": "praktis",
        "comeback": "kebangkitan kembali",
        "passenger": "penumpang",
        "check-in": "lapor diri",
        "reopening": "membuka kembali",
        "greener": "lebih ramah lingkungan"
      },
      "qs": [
